# ZTE B760H device node labels
#
# Both nodes below fell back to the generic `device' type, and granting access
# to `device' is what AOSP's neverallow rejects. Each gets its own type instead.
#
# /dev/mali is created by configs/init/ueventd.mt8127.rc with mode 0666
# system:graphics, so DAC already lets every app open the GPU node - SELinux
# alone was blocking them.
#
# See device.te for the full denial breakdown and for the neverallow that
# forced this approach.
/dev/mali                                    u:object_r:mali_device:s0
/dev/sw_sync                                 u:object_r:sw_sync_b760h_device:s0
